Source: the XML DATA ONLY in lensfunpy/db_files/ shipped with the oracle's
Python environment, measured with lensfun version 0.3.4.0 on 2026-11-13.
Original filenames: 6x6.xml, compact-canon.xml, mil-canon.xml, mil-sony.xml,
mounts.xml, slr-canon.xml, and slr-nikon.xml.
Changes: selected a small subset of lenses/cameras and the required mount
definitions; serialized the selected XML nodes; no calibration values edited.
tools/golden/gen_lens.py reproduces the selection and derived reference cases.

The complete, unmodified database (all 55 XML files of the same folder, Lensfun 0.3.4.0, 4.3 MB) is kept in
data/lensfun/ with its own NOTICE and is embedded in the program (Database::builtin), so the application finds
a lens database with no setup. A user's newer lensfun folder takes precedence. Runtime Rust code requires neither
Python nor the lensfun native library. The CC BY-SA notice and attribution are shown in the About box and in
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

The Rust implementation was independently written using public mathematical/API
documentation and numeric black-box measurements. No lensfun C/C++ source or
lensfunpy binding source was read, copied, translated, linked, or bundled here.
